# Each attribute names work in `ci.yml` that can skip. `build` marks a path whose change
# must start the jobs `rust` and `wheel`, and `scripts` a path whose change must start
# `Scripts` and `Scripts-macOS`. `lint-<lane>` marks a path whose change must start that
# lane of the lint in `Quality`, as .config/lanes names the lanes. For a lane, this file
# marks what its lints read, their own code and the files of mise. `lint-macos` marks a
# path whose change must start `Quality-macOS`: the code of a lint, the files of mise and
# what clippy compiles. `-<attribute>` marks a path whose change need not. `Quality` always
# runs, and only its lanes take an attribute. `Records`, `Commits` and `Sign-off` take none.
#
#   the decision:  docs/decisions/ci-runs-a-lane-of-the-lint-only-when-a-path-it-reads-changes.md
#
# A gate reads the marks on the base branch, so a mark takes effect once it merges.
#
# A pattern that reaches the root, such as `*` or `*.rs`, marks a path before anyone
# decides it, and the lint then passes that path.
#
#   the task:  mise run lint:gates

